+**Scope of this file today.** Plan 3's keystone (Tasks 1–2 plus the coordination doc's §9 rider) and Task 5's hierarchy checks have landed, so only the cases those tasks cover are written down. **Case ids 5.4 through 5.36 are reserved verbatim by Plan 3's own catalogue task** (`docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-20-03-tickets-hierarchy.md`, Task 14) and must not be claimed by anything else — the rest of Plan 3's lane fills them in with the tests that cover them. Task 14's own list also covers Task 5's brief-mandated refusals at 5.7–5.11, 5.21, 5.23 and 5.24; **only the refusals Task 5 minted that no plan document anticipated are catalogued here**, and they continue from 5.38. New cases beyond that continue from 5.44. **Never renumber**: 5.27 and 5.30 are cited by Plan 5, 5.36 by the coordination doc.
 
 - 5.1 ✅ Custom ticket type definitions validated: select needs options, options only on select, duplicate field ids refused, built-in field ids not shadowable, rank ≥ 1. (`packages/domain/test/ticket-types.test.ts`)
 - 5.2 ✅ Built-in ladder ships as seed data with ranks epic 1 / story 2 / task 3 / sub-task 4, materialisable against a workspace default workflow; `DEEPEST_RANK` is asserted against the shipped ladder's real maximum, so a deeper seed fails loudly instead of quietly releasing sub-tasks from the parent requirement. (`packages/domain/test/ticket-types.test.ts`)
 - 5.3 ✅ Every vocabulary event round-trips `parseEvent`; malformed payloads, unknown event types, and a ticket event filed against another kind of entity are all refused at the door. (`packages/domain/test/ticket-events.test.ts`)
